00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.940
It's important to understand
three sections when

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.790
we talk about identity
and access management,

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:45.220
or IAMs on Google Cloud.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.270
The who, does what, and on what.

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:52.840
The who is essentially the
identity part of the IAMs.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.770
The who talks about whether it's
a single user, multiple users

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.680
separately, or multiple
users together.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.800
Multiple users together is
what is referred to as a group,

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.380
and this is what
it is recommended.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:08.680
The does what is the access
or set of access controls

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:12.130
the user has on a particular
set of resource or so.

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:14.950
For example, something
like an admin role

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:18.010
would allow you to
create, modify, delete,

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.840
add other roles, et cetera.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.700
Whereas a viewer
role for a resource

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:23.560
would only allow
you to read from it

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.900
and not modify or delete it.

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.240
And finally, we
have the on what,

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:31.820
which talks about which resource
these obligations are put on.

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:34.570
So let's say a user has
only been granted access

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:37.040
to a particular
Cloud SQL database.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:40.240
This does not allow the user
to access anything apart

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.270
from this particular
Cloud SQL database.

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.360
Here is an example to
understand it as a whole.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.780
There are a group of users who
are granted the access of Cloud

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:55.150
SQL Viewer role, and this grants
them access to the Cloud SQL.

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:58.300
Here are some best
practices regarding IAMs.

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.640
Leverage and understand
the resource hierarchy.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:02.890
Use projects to
group resources that

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:04.630
share the same trust boundary.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.210
Check the policy
granted on each resource

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.170
and make sure you
understand the inheritance.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:13.420
Use the principle of least
privilege, which means,

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:15.700
don't over-provision
any of the permissions

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.920
that a user does not require.

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:21.430
Ground rules to Google Groups
rather than individuals.

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.470
This way, when new
members are added,

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:26.530
they don't have to be permitted
all of those permissions again.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.810
They just need to simply
be added to the group.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:33.010
And finally, use predefined
role whenever possible,

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:36.610
as opposed to basic roles, which
gives us way too much access.

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:38.680
And customize roles
where you need to pick

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.840
and choose from a particular
set of permissions,

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:43.090
which can be hard to maintain.

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:46.660
Let's go over a very short
demonstration for IAM.

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.310
Let's head to the console.

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:51.550
Click on IAM in admin, which
has also been pinned here,

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.980
and make sure you're in IAM.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.930
This is the IAM
dashboard, where you

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.850
can see a bunch of
different permissions

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.860
that have already been assigned.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:04.240
I can add a new role
by either editing here,

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:09.490
by adding a new role, or I can
go ahead and click on Add here.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:12.400
As I want to add it for the
same member, which is myself,

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:17.060
